# {{Project Name}}

> `env.example` — copy to `.env.example` at repo root (and document each var here before a real `.env` exists).
> Rule: **every variable the app reads appears here with a description and a safe placeholder — never a real secret.**

# ── App ──
NODE_ENV=development            # development | production
PORT=3000                       # HTTP port
BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000  # public URL of this instance

# ── Database ──
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/{{db_name}}  # primary DB connection string

# ── Auth ──
SESSION_SECRET={{change-me-32+-random-chars}}   # cookie/session signing key — generate: openssl rand -hex 32

# ── External services (only what the project actually uses) ──
# SUPABASE_URL=https://{{project}}.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY={{server-side-only}}   # never expose to the browser

# ── Errors / observability ──
# SENTRY_DSN=             # error tracking (optional)
